# tinycmdr repo — what is source and what is per-host state.
#
# Rule: anything a host writes for itself (logs, sessions, memory files, secrets,
# backups) never enters git. The same tree is deployed to many hosts, so a committed
# per-host file would read as canonical and be wrong.

# --- per-host state ---
logs/
sessions/
spill/
state.json
# The operator's own theme and persona. The app seeds a missing one from the shipped
# theme.default.toml / soul.example.md at first start, and the host's edited copy must
# never be clobbered by an update - so neither is tracked.
theme.toml
soul.md
*.bak*
web-token.txt
.env
__pycache__/
dist/
# tools/ is per-host tool payload - with ONE exception: the starter tools
# are shipped source (they ride every package), so they are tracked.
tools/*
!tools/patch.py
!tools/process.py
!tools/toolsmith.py
!tools/computer_use.py
!tools/README.md
notes.md
atlas.md
knowledge/
skills/.imported-unused/

# --- more per-host state and scratch artifacts ---
# Every name here is a file a host writes for itself, or a scratch artifact.
field-notes.md
# the field-note hit counters: per-host state, written on every failure the harness sees
field-notes-hits.json
notes-archive.md
notes-authored.json
# the confirm gate's approvals (per-host: what the operator told it to stop asking)
confirm-allow.json
tests/eval-runs/
snapshots/
tmp/
uploads/
.archive/
.pre-*
*.pre-*
config.json
jobs.json
inbox/
*.log
# A rotated log keeps a numeric suffix, and `*` stops at the dot, so `git add -A` in a
# live tree would commit a host log. Both names belong here for the same reason.
*.log.*
*.lock
*.tmp
skills/
.env.*
!.env.example
web-token.txt.*
web-sessions.json
# the tools/ provenance record written at run start (ToolRegistry.note_provenance)
tools-provenance.json
a.txt
lines.txt*

# Host-specific operational tooling & notes
maintenance/atlas-notes/
# Engineering notes: they name hosts, addresses and the operator's
# decisions, so they are never shipped and never committed.
docs/dev-log.md
docs/deferred-corrections.md
maintenance/fleet-version-report.ps1
maintenance/fleet-metrics.py
maintenance/register-boot-recovery.ps1
maintenance/start-containers.ps1
maintenance/task-audit.ps1
docs/handoff-*.md
docs/staged-*.md
# A pre-edit copy of a build: a whole build, not source, so it is a scratch
# artifact.
probe-pre.py
launch_tinycmdr.bat
tinycmdr-service.vbs

# The private inventory (host names, ids, addresses, secret labels).
# build-package.py refuses to build a public package without it.
maintenance/private_rules.py

# maintenance/where.py's per-host tree declaration: it names this box's own paths
# (a backup share, an ops workspace), which are true of one machine and nobody else.
maintenance/where-roles.json

# --- common live-tree clutter: on a real host these show up as untracked, which
# makes `git status` useless for spotting real drift.
venv/
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
# --- more live-tree clutter, found by maintenance/where.py, for the same reason ---
# experiments.jsonl is written by the run itself; the tool-audit folder is a
# per-host evidence dump. Neither is source, and both make `git status` in a live
# tree look dirty next to a REAL tracked modification - the two are told apart.
experiments.jsonl
maintenance/tool-audit-*/
# the browser auto-open marker (one tab per token+port per window)
.web-open
